p('<b>Question answered.</b> Yes: an incidence-conditioned replacement improves on two on explicit sparse nontrivial QC-GHP families beyond B1, with a reusable bound and a separate exact-six family. <b>Still open in this checkpoint.</b> The best possible general incidence bound, tight stopping distances of the powers-of-three family, and stronger spectral bounds on classes distinguishable from the bad counterparts. <b>Next decisive step.</b> Tighten the spectral comparison and the incidence criterion while retaining faithful binary, cover and Lean interfaces. This is a bounded stronger-bound result, not a universal resolution of every meaning of the source’s broad research direction.')
